---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE, COMPANY } from '../data/site';

const lastUpdated = 'September 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How MA Utility Solutions collects, uses and protects your personal data, in line with UK GDPR. Covers data we collect, third parties, cookies, retention and your rights."
>
  <section class="bg-navy">
    <div class="container-page section-padding text-center">
      <span class="eyebrow-inverse">Legal</span>
      <h1 class="mx-auto mt-5 max-w-2xl text-4xl font-extrabold text-white sm:text-5xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-white/60">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-padding">
    <div class="container-page">
      <div class="prose-content mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-10 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-light sm:text-base">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold text-navy sm:text-2xl">1. Who we are</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            {SITE.name} ("we", "us", "our") is an independent UK brokerage helping homeowners and businesses find
            better deals on energy, water, solar and building trades. This policy explains how we collect, use and
            protect your personal data when you use our website or contact us, in line with the UK General Data
            Protection Regulation (UK GDPR) and the Data Protection Act 2018.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The data controller is {COMPANY.legalName}, a company registered in {COMPANY.registeredIn} (company
            number {COMPANY.number}), registered office {COMPANY.registeredOffice}. We are registered with the Information
            Commissioner's Office under registration number {COMPANY.icoNumber}.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You can contact us about anything in this policy at
            <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="font-semibold text-amber-ink hover:underline">{SITE.email}</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold text-navy sm:text-2xl">2. What data we collect</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">We only collect data that you provide to us directly, primarily through our contact and feedback forms. This may include:</p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
            <li>Name</li>
            <li>Email address</li>
            <li>Phone number</li>
            <li>Postcode</li>
            <li>Whether your enquiry is for a home or a business, and your business name if you give it</li>
            <li>Service(s) you're interested in or have used</li>
            <li>Your current supplier and contract end date, if you choose to share them</li>
            <li>Details of your enquiry or feedback you choose to share</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            When you use one of our forms, our spam protection (Cloudflare Turnstile — see section 4) also processes
            limited technical information from your browser and device, such as your IP address.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We do not collect financial, banking or payment card details through our website, and we never ask for
            passwords or account credentials for your existing suppliers.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold text-navy sm:text-2xl">3. How we use your data</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">We use the data you provide to:</p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
            <li>Respond to your enquiry and arrange a consultation</li>
            <li>Compare deals across the market on your behalf, once authorised (e.g. via a Letter of Authority)</li>
            <li>Manage your account and any ongoing service with us</li>
            <li>Improve our website and services based on feedback</li>
            <li>Meet our legal, regulatory and contractual obligations</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">Our legal bases for using your data are:</p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
            <li>
              <strong class="text-navy">Taking steps before a contract, and performing it</strong> — when you ask us
              about our services, and once you engage us (UK GDPR Article 6(1)(b)).
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-navy">Legitimate interests</strong> — responding to enquiries and feedback, keeping
              our forms free of spam, and running and improving our business (Article 6(1)(f)).
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-navy">Legal obligation</strong> — keeping records we're required to keep by law
              (Article 6(1)(c)).
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-navy">Consent</strong> — only where we specifically ask for it, such as the optional
              tick-box allowing us to publish your feedback as a testimonial. You can withdraw consent at any time.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold text-navy sm:text-2xl">4. Who we share data with</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">We only share personal data where necessary, and never sell it. Third parties we may share data with include:</p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
            <li><strong class="text-navy">Form processing service (Web3Forms)</strong> — used to route enquiry and feedback form submissions to us.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-navy">Microsoft 365</strong> — used for email and, for business customers, appointment booking via Microsoft Bookings.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-navy">Cloudflare</strong> — our website hosting and content delivery provider. We also use Cloudflare Web Analytics to count visits and measure how quickly our pages load (see section 5).</li>
            <li><strong class="text-navy">Cloudflare Turnstile</strong> — spam protection on our contact and feedback forms. It checks that a real person, not an automated bot, is submitting the form, using technical information from your browser and device such as your IP address.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-navy">Energy, water and solar suppliers</strong> — only where you have authorised us to act on your behalf (e.g. via a Letter of Authority), and only to the extent needed to obtain comparisons or process a switch.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">We do not share your data with third parties for their own marketing purposes.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Some of these providers (Web3Forms, Microsoft and Cloudflare) may process data outside the UK. Where they
            do, we rely on safeguards recognised under UK data protection law, such as the UK International Data
            Transfer Agreement or Addendum, or the UK–US data bridge.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold text-navy sm:text-2xl">5. Cookies and external resources</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Our website keeps things simple: we do not use cookies for analytics or advertising, and we do not track
            you across other websites. Everything on our pages — including fonts — is served from our own website,
            apart from two Cloudflare services:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
            <li>
              <strong class="text-navy">Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong> — on every page, to count visits and
              measure page speed. It doesn't use cookies or build a profile of you; it processes limited technical
              information (such as your IP address, browser and the page you visited) to produce overall statistics.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-navy">Cloudflare Turnstile</strong> — on our contact and feedback pages only, to
              protect the forms from spam (see section 4).
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold text-navy sm:text-2xl">6. Data retention</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">We keep personal data only for as long as we need it:</p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
            <li>
              <strong class="text-navy">Enquiries that don't lead to working together</strong> — up to 12 months
              from your last contact with us, so we can follow up or pick up where we left off if you get back in
              touch.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-navy">Clients</strong> — for as long as we work together, then 6 years after our
              relationship ends, to meet legal, accounting and regulatory requirements and to deal with any claims.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-navy">Feedback</strong> — kept for internal review in line with the periods above.
              If you consented to it being published as a testimonial, you can withdraw that consent at any time and
              we'll remove it from our website.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold text-navy sm:text-2xl">7. Your rights</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">Under UK GDPR, you have the right to:</p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
            <li>Access the personal data we hold about you</li>
            <li>Request correction of inaccurate data</li>
            <li>Request erasure of your data, in certain circumstances</li>
            <li>Object to or restrict certain processing</li>
            <li>Withdraw consent at any time, where processing is based on consent</li>
            <li>Request a copy of your data in a portable format</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            To exercise any of these rights, email us at
            <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="font-semibold text-amber-ink hover:underline">{SITE.email}</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold text-navy sm:text-2xl">8. Complaints</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            If you're unhappy with how we've handled your data, please contact us first via our
            <a href="/complaints" class="font-semibold text-amber-ink hover:underline">Complaints Procedure</a> page
            so we can try to put things right. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the UK's
            supervisory authority, the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO), at
            <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="font-semibold text-amber-ink hover:underline">ico.org.uk</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold text-navy sm:text-2xl">9. Contact us</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            {COMPANY.legalName} (trading as {SITE.name})<br />
            Registered office: {COMPANY.registeredOffice}<br />
            Email: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="font-semibold text-amber-ink hover:underline">{SITE.email}</a><br />
            Website: <a href={SITE.url} class="font-semibold text-amber-ink hover:underline">{SITE.url.replace('https://', '')}</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
